# Fundraising Lookup OTP email

## Invariant

Opening a valid Lookup link auto-emails one code. **Resend verification code must send a new email** (short double-click debounce only). Failed code entry must not restart the email cooldown.

`updated_at` on `fundraising_lookup_otps` is last **issue** time, not last verify attempt.

## Why Resend looked broken

1. Page load minted/sent OTP (`reason: auto`, 60s cooldown).
2. Partner typed an old/wrong code → verify used to bump `updated_at`.
3. Resend reused that timestamp as “just sent” and skipped email (`emailed: false`).
4. If the first send failed after upsert, cooldown still blocked retry until discard.

## Required behaviour

| Path | Email |
|------|--------|
| Auto (page load / Strict Mode) | Skip if issued < 60s and still valid |
| Manual Resend | Send unless issued < 12s (double-click) |
| Attempts ≥ 5 or expired | Always mint + send |
| Resend API send failure | Delete unsent OTP so retry is immediate |

Client POST body: `{ token, reason: 'auto' | 'manual' }`.

## Cousins

- Invalid/rotated token (Reset Access Link) → 400, no email
- Inactive partner → same
- Previous codes die when a new OTP is minted — copy must say use the latest email
- Spam folder / wrong `contactEmail`
- Localhost vs `www.selpic.com.au` Lookup URL (partner-facing host rule)

